                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm somewhat surprised there hasn't been some sort of official fix for this but reading over https://bugs.launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/apparmor/+bug/2056555, it seems like we're just left to fend for ourselves. Disabling this globally doesn't really seem right, but bitbake gotta work."
                },
                {
                    "file": "setup",
                    "line": 139,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "1. I'm not super keen on having something for a particular version of a particular Linux distribution in our setup script forever.  I get 24.04 is the current LTS of Ubuntu, so maybe it is slightly acceptable.\n\n2. Reading the bug (https://bugs.launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/apparmor/+bug/2056555), it sounds like all Ubuntu versions after this fix it by having a prompt to the user to allow the action.  Is that true?  If that is true can we restrict this to 24.04 specifically?  \n\n3. Just checking for apparmor_restrict_unpriviledged_userns doesn't seem appropriate if we're not also tying this to distributions / versions that have this issue."
                },
                {
                    "file": "setup",
                    "line": 139,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "AKash-A007",
                        "email": "mirrorghost007@gmail.com",
                        "username": "AKash-A007"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "setup",
                    "line": 146,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Shouldn't we warn that this is potentially a security impact?  You're explicitly disabling all security, in this space, for your entire Linux system.  Most people would just blindly copy whatever you tell them."
                },
                {
                    "file": "setup",
                    "line": 146,
                    "reviewer": {
